## Exact source-surface rule

For an `ok` row, copy the complete unit or named metric from the shortest exact
source phrase that defines the selected value. Do not paraphrase it, expand an
abbreviation, change singular/plural, add isotope labels, replace a slash with a
hyphen, or add explanatory words. A nonempty `unit_text` must be copied verbatim.
If two source phrases could name the metric and neither is uniquely selected,
return `unsure` rather than choosing or rewriting one.

Do not rescue one number from a measurement string that itself presents `vs`,
`from ... to ...`, a semicolon-separated pair, or several equally focal results.
Such a row is `unsure` unless the selected result is explicitly relative, in
which case it is `relative`.
